      "content": "An escrow agent acts as a neutral third party in a real estate transaction, holding funds and documents safely between the buyer and seller. They ensure all contractual conditions are met before releasing the money to the seller and the deed to the buyer. This prevents both parties from losing their money or the property due to misunderstanding or failure to comply with the contract terms. Essentially, they manage the transaction to keep things fair and secure until everything is finalized.",
