      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it seems counterintuitive, escrow companies are highly regulated financial professionals with strict protocols to protect the funds. They are not typically \"sitting on\" the money carelessly; rather, they are safeguarding it according to the specific terms and timelines laid out in the contract. The risk is heavily mitigated because the escrow agent only releases funds when *all* agreed-upon conditions, like clear title or final inspections, have been officially met.",
