      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Escrow companies are licensed and insured, operating under strict legal oversight to prevent misuse or loss of client funds. They must maintain separate, designated escrow accounts, meaning the transaction money does not get mixed with the company's general operating funds. If an agent were to mismanage the funds, there are strong legal safeguards and insurance policies in place to protect the buyer and seller.",
